<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hattusili I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hattusili I was an early king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a>, regarded as one of the founders of the Hittite kingdom. He is associated with making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> the capital and with campaigns into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. His reign marks the foundation of the Hittite Empire as a regional power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hattusili-i.jpg" alt="Hattusili I" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA; colorized and wording by Laszlovszky András at Hungarian Wikipedia based on Világtörténet tíz kötetben, Kossuth Könyvkiadó, 1962 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korahettita_id%C5%91szak_t%C3%A9rk%C3%A9pe.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
